      "answer": "On Cryptopsy's Once Was Not (2005), Flo Mounier played a Yamaha Recording Custom kit — a significant departure from the Pearl Masters BRX of his 2000 album And Then You'll Beg. The Yamaha Recording Custom's 7-ply birch shell construction produces a faster attack transient and tighter resonance compared to Pearl's maple/birch hybrid, a sonic characteristic suited to the extreme velocities Once Was Not demanded. The configuration included a 22-inch bass drum (returning to a smaller shell after the 26-inch experiment of And Then You'll Beg), 10-inch and 12-inch rack toms, and 14-inch and 16-inch floor toms. The smaller bass drum delivered faster attack response for the album's 270+ BPM blast sequences."
