              "text": "On Cryptopsy's Once Was Not (2005), Flo Mounier played a Yamaha Recording Custom kit with 7-ply birch shells. The configuration included a 22-inch bass drum, 10-inch and 12-inch rack toms, and 14-inch and 16-inch floor toms. This represented a significant departure from the Pearl Masters BRX he had used on And Then You'll Beg (2000)."
